{"diagnosis": "Fetch makes no progress: max_addr stays 0x00000000 instead of advancing through the 256-word NOP memory, causing TRAP: no progress and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Expected reg_next_pc to advance to the next fetch address each cycle. Root cause in excerpt at lines 1526-1527 is reg_next_pc <= current_pc copying the current PC with no increment, so reg_pc never advances.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1527,1 +1527,1 @@
-				reg_next_pc <= current_pc;
+				reg_next_pc <= current_pc + 4;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), progress with max_addr advancing through NOPs and trap on end-of-mem"}

